  The words of the errors of the uploads of a ResumableUploadField, which Wicket's
  ResumableUploadToResourceField looks for with the limits of the field and of its resource:
  ${fileMaxSize}, ${maxUploadsPerSession} and ${maxBytesPerSession}. The rows of the files show
  them as well, by the keys the server tells.
-->
<properties>
	<entry key="wicket.no.files.selected">Nothing to upload: no files were chosen.</entry>
	<entry key="uploadSingleFileTooLarge">A file weighs more than ${fileMaxSize}, the most for a file.</entry>
	<entry key="uploadToResourceFailed">The upload failed.</entry>
	<entry key="uploadConnectionLost">The connection to the server broke off during the upload.</entry>
	<entry key="resumableUploadTooLarge">Larger than ${fileMaxSize}, the most for a file.</entry>
	<entry key="resumableUploadTooMany">${maxUploadsPerSession} uploads at once at most: finish or cancel one first.</entry>
	<entry key="resumableUploadTooMuch">The uploads not finished yet would weigh more than ${maxBytesPerSession} together.</entry>
	<entry key="resumableUploadNoRoom">The server has no room for the file now: try again later.</entry>
	<entry key="resumableUploadLost">The server no longer has the upload: choose the file again.</entry>
</properties>
